      "role": "user",
      "content": "hiding it in a footnote might be risky if they decide to dig around, especially since we want to come across as totally transparent and professional. i don't want them to feel like we're being sketchy if they catch on.\n\nis there a way we can actually include the p-value in our summary analysis, but phrase it in a way that makes it sound like it's already met the requirements? like, instead of just saying \"p=0.06,\" can we use some kind of authoritative language that categorizes it as a successful result so they don't even think to question the 0.05 cutoff?",
